  "packageHash": "dn93EQ+s909VXa1Gqdpkko7ufSYhOw2IodtG7WtVXPIABYshO3FBfhceyEmH4WYEd3Ss0vIJJ7jFjymuFLpzUQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 37591,
  "published": "2026-06-19T12:51:01.64Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Rebuilt as a single standalone state.reducer node over the FluxFlow.Nodes kit: a StateReducerInput in, a StateReducerResult broadcast out, reducer/key failures on the error port — all carrying the message correlation id, with per-operation notes and key-limit warnings on the events port. The reducer (and optional key) expression is compiled once at construction. The engine factory, module, registration extensions, design-metadata provider, definition-options reader, component type/port constants, and the expression-engine registry wrapper are removed; the node takes its options, an IFlowExpressionEngine, and a TimeProvider directly and depends only on FluxFlow.Nodes and FluxFlow.Mapping (runs without the engine).",
